 "response": "Driril's budget is now **$1,528K**. I tracked every budget update in order, starting from $1,630K (#0001).\n\n**Approach**\n- Only Finance Office budget updates count. Messages from other teams, and Finance notes that don't change the budget (room moves, audit notes, cost-center changes), were ignored.\n- For each withdrawal chain, I worked out which withdrawals still stand. A withdrawal counts only if it has not itself been withdrawn. A budget update is removed only if a withdrawal that still stands targets it.\n\n**Examples of chains that change the result**\n- **#0004 (+$237K) stays.** Its withdrawal #0019 was itself withdrawn by #0114.\n- **#0024 (+$502K) stays.** The chain runs #0566 \u2192 #0116 \u2192 #0047 \u2192 #0032. Because #0566 stands, #0116 is cancelled, so #0047 stands and cancels #0032.\n- **#0009 is removed.** #1018 cancels #0075, so #0056 stands and withdraws #0009.\n- **#0473 is removed.** In the chain #1039 \u2192 #0924 \u2192 #0720 \u2192 #0631 \u2192 #0571, #0571 ends up standing and withdraws #0473.\n- **#0214 (\u2212$571K) stays.** #1596 cancels #1006, so #0254 stands and cancels #0225.\n- **#0442 is removed.** #1428 cancels #1409, so #0735 stands and withdraws #0442.\n\nAll remaining updates were applied once, in order, to reach $1,528K. I did not do a second independent recount, so the total relies on a single careful pass.\n\nANSWER: $1528K",
